ship and he was laying down, and was fast asleep."},{"verse":6,"text":"So the ship master came to him, and said to him, “What do you mean, sleeper? Arise, call on your God! Maybe your God will notice us, so that we won’t perish.”"},{"verse":7,"text":"They all said to each other, “Come! Let’s cast lots, that we may know who is responsible for this evil that is on us.” So they cast lots, and the lot fell on Jonah."},{"verse":8,"text":"Then they asked him, “Tell us, please, for whose cause this evil is on us. What is your occupation? Where do you come from? What is your country? Of what people are you?”"},{"verse":9,"text":"He said to them, “I am a Hebrew, and I fear the LORD, the God of heaven, who has made the sea and the dry land.”"},{"verse":10,"text":"Then the men were exceedingly afraid, and said to him, “What have you done?” For the men knew that he was fleeing from the presence of the LORD, because he had told them."},{"verse":11,"text":"Then they said to him, “What shall we do to you, that the sea may be calm to us?” For the sea grew more and more stormy."},{"verse":12,"text":"He said to them, “Take me up, and throw me into the sea. Then the sea will be calm for you; for I know that because of me this great storm is on you.”"},{"verse":13,"text":"Nevertheless the men rowed hard to get them back to the land; but they could not, for the sea grew more and more stormy against them."},{"verse":14,"text":"Therefore they cried to the LORD, and said, “We beg you, LORD, we beg you, don’t let us die for this man’s life, and don’t lay on us innocent blood; for you, LORD, have done as it pleased you.”"},{"verse":15,"text":"So they took up Jonah and threw him into the sea; and the sea ceased its raging."},{"verse":16,"text":"Then the men feared the LORD exceedingly; and they offered a sacrifice to the LORD and made vows."},{"verse":17,"text":"The LORD prepared a huge fish to swallow up Jonah, and Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights."}],"hasArtwork":false,"availableLangs":[]}]